      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_9df68df523344c98ed5105c4498a11baa8d9f3ef8abffb34e0d4bf5c150188bb",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "After the universal leading escape geometry is cancelled, nontrivial denominator-zeta zeros control the next small-hole scale. The source states two iterated-limit criteria—one for a normalized one-hole remainder and one comparing one hole with twice the symmetric two-hole escape—and each holds for every positive delta exactly when RH holds. This translates horizontal zero location into a correction exponent, but it is a mathematical equivalence of limits rather than an experimental proof; rational two-hole analogues are conditional on the corresponding finite set of GRH statements.",
