    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_5a499dafde7b5cf8b8d332223a7868765ec160692f7febe3d48111ebaa1321bc",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Angular-momentum conservation reduces the circle billiard to fixed boundary rotations, making coprime rational angles the periodic skeleton around which long-lived trajectories slowly precess. Measuring those resonant neighborhoods converts the geometric survival problem into the totient–Möbius coefficient of a finite orbit sum, and Mellin transformation then converts its small-hole scaling into residue data. This dynamical-to-arithmetic-to-meromorphic chain is available only by combining the rotation classification, long-time neighborhood calculation, and Mellin representation.",
