    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_a770ffc46ee974fd75982f42dd22d8bab9126cb3ab9af5553596fd1ac1fa72cb",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The exact escape coefficient is represented as a residue sum whose pole sources can be separated. Elementary real poles alone yield an analytic integer-power expansion and cannot express the exact staircase; nonreal poles inherited from zeta zeros provide the missing nonsmooth structure. Residue-truncation plots then diagnose this representational dependence by showing where additional real poles or additional critical-line poles are needed at different hole scales.",
