    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_b64e7791fc9295011fd7167144199e6ef14c133242fe14ce67c2e447ac863133",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "A rational hole separation supplies finite residue-class symmetry modulo its denominator, so character orthogonality diagonalizes the orbit sum into finitely many Dirichlet L-function ratios. The denominator L-function zeros then become poles of the Mellin integrand and control zero-sensitive correction scales after the universal leading geometry is removed: the source gives RH-equivalent limits in the one-hole and symmetric-two-hole comparison and ties rational two-hole corrections to the relevant finite GRH family. Irrational separation loses this finite spectral decomposition; equidistribution and arithmetic means recover the universal leading term while finer analytic structure remains unresolved.",
